  "seoBody": "<h2>Is GoAudits a good product?</h2><p>Yes. We will say that plainly. GoAudits is a mature inspection and audit app with an excellent template library, clean and configurable PDF reporting, a clear completion dashboard, and UK-based support. The price is competitive, from around £10 per seat per month, which sits well below the enterprise tools. For a UK firm that wants a capable inspection app without an enterprise bill, GoAudits is a reasonable default.</p><p>So the honest reason firms go looking for a GoAudits alternative is rarely that GoAudits is weak. It is that GoAudits is still an app with a login, and for some teams the app itself is the barrier.</p><h2>The one structural limit</h2><p>GoAudits is an app. Every worker downloads it and keeps a login alive. For a desk-based or adoption-tolerant team that is a non-issue and GoAudits works well.</p><p>For a team out on jobs, an app is one more thing to open when hands are full. The inspection gets done. GoAudits gets filled in later, in the van or the car park, from memory. The record says completed. It reflects what someone remembered, not what they observed in real time.</p><p>A cheaper app does not fix this, because the friction was never the price. It was the act of opening an app and logging in at the point of work.</p><h2>The alternatives</h2><h3>GoAudits</h3><p>The app-based option done well: good templates, clean reports, UK support, low price. Pick it when the team will use an app. It does not solve an adoption problem that comes from resistance to opening an app at all.</p><h3>Paper and spreadsheets</h3><p>Still common in UK teams. Free, familiar, no training. The records are illegible, unsearchable, and impossible to produce when a client or regulator asks. The cost is not the subscription. It is the liability when the folder cannot be found.</p><h3>Quickler</h3><p>Quickler runs in WhatsApp. There is nothing to install and no login. The inspection workflow arrives in the worker's existing WhatsApp chat, and they reply to each question as a message, the same way they reply to anything else. Voice notes are transcribed automatically. The core output is a shareable web report and a permanent record, with optional PDF and CSV export.</p><p>Pricing is only for active users: [[price:bundles]]. An active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, so you add your whole team and only pay for who actually works. Everything is unlimited on a paid account.</p><p>The honest limitation: quickler is not a drag-and-drop form builder and does not have thousands of pre-built templates. For complex, branching audits with sophisticated scoring logic, GoAudits is the more flexible product. Quickler is built for teams of roughly 1 to 30 doing structured compliance and inspection capture. Rooted in UK compliance, it works anywhere WhatsApp does. If your team will happily use an app, GoAudits is a mature choice and there is no reason to switch.</p><h2>Direct comparison</h2><p><strong>GoAudits:</strong> per seat, from ~£10/seat/mo; app install and login required; UK-focused team.</p><p><strong>iAuditor:</strong> per seat, from ~£19/seat/mo; app install and login required; global support, UK timezone covered.</p><p><strong>Lumiform:</strong> per seat, from ~£12/seat/mo; app install and login required; European HQ, UK customers served.</p><p><strong>Quickler:</strong> £20 per active user/mo, dormant users free, only pay for who works; WhatsApp only, no install; UK-based, direct founder contact.</p><p>Pricing is approximate. Check each vendor's current pricing before deciding.</p><h2>How to choose</h2><p>The deciding test is simple: will your team open an app on site, or not.</p><p>If they will, GoAudits is a good, cheaper answer with mature templates and UK support. There is no reason to switch away from something that works.</p><p>If they will not, and people fill forms later from memory because opening an app is one step too many, a WhatsApp-native workflow removes the barrier because they already use WhatsApp for everything else.</p><p><strong>One thing to check before switching:</strong> does the alternative produce a report format your clients and regulators will accept? PDF output from any reputable tool should be fine for most purposes, but verify if your sector has specific requirements.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Is GoAudits any good?</h3><p>Yes. GoAudits is a mature, well-priced inspection app with strong templates, clean reporting and UK-based support. If your team will use an app, it is a sensible, proven choice.</p><h3>What is the difference between GoAudits and Quickler?</h3><p>GoAudits is a dedicated inspection app: install, log in, complete forms inside it. Quickler runs in WhatsApp: the worker receives questions in their existing chat and replies. GoAudits has a larger template library and a more flexible form builder. Quickler has higher on-site completion because there is no app to open and no login to remember.</p><h3>Is Quickler cheaper than GoAudits?</h3><p>It depends on your team shape. GoAudits charges per seat, from around £10 a seat a month. Quickler charges £20 per active user a month, where an active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, and dormant users are free. A team with many occasional users often pays less on quickler. A small team where everyone is active every month may pay less on GoAudits.</p><h3>Should I switch from GoAudits to Quickler?</h3><p>Only if adoption is your problem. If your team happily opens the GoAudits app on site, stay put. If people fill forms later from memory because opening an app is one step too many, test a WhatsApp-native workflow. Quickler has a free tier of 20 reports a month, up to 10 photos per report, no card and no trial clock.</p><h2>Try this in Quickler</h2><p>Start free, no card, no trial clock. Copy and paste this into the workflow description when you sign up at <a href=\"https://app.quickler.co/signup\">app.quickler.co/signup</a>:</p><p><code>GoAudits alternative. Workflow name: [Your GoAudits template name]. Description: Describe the inspection template you use most in GoAudits. Include: what is being inspected, number of questions, whether photos are required, and what the output looks like. Quickler rebuilds your template as a WhatsApp workflow. £20 per active user a month, dormant users free, only pay for who works.</code></p><p>Quickler reads your description and builds the WhatsApp question sequence. Your team answers on site. Report produced automatically.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/iauditor-alternative-uk.html\">iAuditor alternative UK</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/safetyculture-alternative-uk.html\">SafetyCulture alternative UK</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/lumiform-alternative-uk.html\">Lumiform alternative UK</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/alternatives.html\">All comparisons</a></li></ul>",
